    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15241": {
      "title": "Faculty (Teaching or Tenure Track) - Radiological Science",
      "description": "Gannon University | Faculty (Teaching or Tenure Track) - Radiological Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Faculty (Teaching or Tenure Track) - Radiological Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Faculty (Teaching or Tenure Track) - Radiological Science Posting Number F252P Division School of Health Professions Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Radiologic Sciences Department is seeking a full-time faculty member. This position is responsible for teaching in the Radiologic Science program, lecture courses and clinical experiences, and assisting with accreditation. The faculty member is responsible to the Program Director and the Dean of Morosky College of Health Professions and Sciences for fulfilling both teaching and non-teaching activities. This is a full-time 12-month teaching track position. The successful applicant is expected to implement course materials that support stated initiatives and use appropriate techniques to provide students with the knowledge needed to achieve the learning outcomes for each course offered. The functions below are detailed in the faculty handbook in Volume IV of the Institutional Policy Manual. 1. Teach 27 credit hours in the academic year or as otherwise specified by the faculty member’s appointment notice; student course evaluations are to be completed in each course. Faculty are expected to employ sound pedagogical practices and to use technology as appropriate, including the University’s learning management system. Faculty shall assist with course revisions and curriculum development as needed. 2. Achieve appropriate student-learning outcomes in all courses taught. 3. Participate in service to the University, the community and to their profession. Attend convocations, commencement exercises and community meetings. 4. Participate in ongoing professional development. 5. Assist, advise and mentor students enrolled in the University. 6. Assist and contribute to the outcomes assessment required for program accreditation by the JRCERT . 6. Fulfill the essential duties and responsibilities of a faculty member as described in Volume IV of the Gannon University Institutional Policy Manual which contains the approved policies and procedures of the University concerning the terms and conditions of faculty employment at the University. Required Qualifications Graduate of a JRCERT accredited Radiologic Sciences program. Minimum of five (5) years’ experience in radiologic sciences profession. Licenses and Certifications: Must be a registered technologist (R.T.) that is licensed, and in good standing with the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists ( ARRT ). University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its strong liberal arts foundation that supports exemplary professional education programs. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree preferred or willing to continue pursuit of a bachelor’s degree recommended. Experience teaching in an accredited Radiologic Science program. Additional certifications in computed tomography (CT), magnetic resonance imaging ( MRI ), or other areas of the radiologic sciences is a plus. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy academic program and environment. Tenure Status Teaching Track Position Type Regular Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Credits Per Year 27 Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Teaching Statement Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15216": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Clinical Coordinator in Physician Assistant (Ruskin, FL)",
      "description": "Gannon University | Assistant Professor/Clinical Coordinator in Physician Assistant (Ruskin, FL) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor/Clinical Coordinator in Physician Assistant (Ruskin, FL) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Professor/Clinical Coordinator in Physician Assistant (Ruskin, FL) Posting Number F256P Division School of Health Professions Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Ruskin, Fl Position Summary Gannon University’s Morosky College of Health Professions and Sciences invites applications for a full-time Clinical Coordinator and faculty member in the Physician Assistant Program in Ruskin, Florida. The appointment for this twelve-month, tenure-track or teaching-track position begins as early as October 2026. Responsibilities include identifying and developing clinical sites, working with clinical year students according to established standards, preparation of student examinations, and providing research guidance to graduate-level students. The successful candidate will be expected to work collaboratively with colleagues, support an interprofessional learning environment, teach and advise students, and participate in service activities to support the University, community, and profession. Qualified candidates will be expected to engage in scholarly activities in keeping with the Boyer Model of Scholarship as appropriate to the application and receipt of tenure and promotion at Gannon. Gannon University seeks excellence through inclusiveness and invites members of underrepresented groups to apply. Required Qualifications Education/Experience: Master of Physician Assistant Science degree (or equivalent) or a medical degree (M.D. or D.O.) is required; two-to-five (2-5) years of full-time clinical experience is required. Rank: In accordance with the University’s standards, the Provost and Vice President for Student Experience awards initial rank at the time of employment. Licenses and Certifications: Current NCCPA certification is preferable; candidates must have or be eligible for PA, MD, or DO licensure in Florida. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its strong liberal arts foundation that supports exemplary professional education programs. Preferred Qualifications Candidates with a post-professional doctorate degree (PhD, DSc, DHSc, EdD, etc.) are preferred. A minimum of two (2) years of teaching, clinical preceptor, and/or research experience are preferred. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy academic environment. Work is performed in a busy classroom and office setting. Travel to clinical sites may be necessary on occasion. Tenure Status Tenure Track Position Type Regular Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Credits Per Year 24 (tenure track) or 27 (teaching track) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Statement Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
