ar re-accreditation through the Commission on Accreditation in Physical Therapy Education ( CAPTE ). The program is face-to-face, 9 semesters in length, and requires 111 credits for completion. The curriculum is systems based and service-focused, emphasizing didactic to clinical competency in the development of a strong entry-level generalist physical therapist. Required Qualifications Education/Experience Requirements: Qualified candidates will possess a post-professional doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DHS , DSc, etc. or ABD ) and/or a DPT degree. Candidate’s content expertise will be used to assign teaching load. Additional requirements include greater than three years of clinical experience, three years of clinical teaching as a clinical instructor and/or site coordinator of clinical education. License : Must be eligible for Florida state licensure as a physical therapist. Rank : In accordance with the University’s standards, the Provost and Vice President for Student Experience will award initial rank at the time of hire. University Mission : Must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its strong liberal arts foundation that supports exemplary professional education programs. Preferred Qualifications ABPTS specialty certification Expertise in musculoskeletal physical therapy Expertise in exercise physiology Prior teaching experience in an entry-level PT program Research experience Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy academic environment. Tenure Status Tenure Track Position Type Regular Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Credits Per Year 24 (tenure track) or 27 (teaching track) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
