    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15175": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Master&#39;s of Business Administration, Business Analytics",
      "description": "Gannon University | Adjunct Faculty - Master&#39;s of Business Administration, Business Analytics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty - Master's of Business Administration, Business Analytics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. A list of courses in the program is below. Please indicate your preference for a specific course(s) when you apply. GMBA615 Technological Environment of Business GMBA625 Data Driven Strategic Planning & Decision-Making GMBA635 Financial Management & Modeling GMBA645 Strategic Global Marketing & Analytics GMBA655 Socially Responsible Leadership GMBA665 Operations & Supply Chain Analytics GMBA675 Managing Organizational Behavior and Dynamics GMBA685 Organizational Communication & Data Visualization GMBA695 Entrepreneurship in a Technological Environment GMBA725 Integrated Business Strategy & Analytics Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Adjunct Faculty - Master's of Business Administration, Business Analytics Posting Number AP042 Division School of Business Department Col. of Engineering & Business Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Gannon University’s Dahlkemper School of Business continually accepts applications for adjunct faculty in the on-site Masters of Business Administration ( MBA ) program with a focus in Business Analytics. Required Qualifications Required Qualifications & Specific needs are as follows: Ideal candidates will hold a doctoral degree in business, computer science or a related field. In addition to the doctoral degree, candidates having either prior teaching experience and/or professional experience in business analytics will be given preference. Adjunct faculty must have on-site availability (Center for Business Ingenuity, 900 State Street, Erie, PA); classes are one evening a week from 6:00 to 8:50 PM for the duration of a 14-week semester. Classes run in the fall, spring and summer semesters. Candidates must successfully execute on the overall program objectives (below) as well as specific course outcomes: Identification of external variables and technological factors that influence business performance and operations Analysis and development of robust business models Use of analytics-related software is required. Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate will have a Doctorate or Master’s degree with teaching or extensive professional business experience. Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a normal academic environment. WORKING CONDITIONS Work is performed in a normal classroom and office setting. Tenure Status Temporary Position Type Adjunct Faculty Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 5M Credits Per Year 1-6 Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
