    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15144": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology",
      "description": "Gannon University | Adjunct Instructor of Biology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Instructor of Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Adjunct Instructor of Biology Posting Number AP021 Division School of Sciences Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Department of Biology seeks individuals interested in teaching non-majors and majors courses as Adjunct Instructors. Teaching loads depend on departmental needs each semester, but may include anatomy & physiology and other organismal courses. Adjuncts typically teach 1–3 sections each term, often during weekday afternoons and evenings. Applicants should upload a cover letter and resume/CV highlighting any previous teaching experience. Required Qualifications A masters degree in BIology or closely related field. Previous teaching is preferred but not required. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Applicants should be able to perform typical actions involved in an academic lab setting, including lifting up to 25 pounds and moving through a lab environment. Applicants must be able to teach face-to-face classes on the Erie campus. Tenure Status Temporary Position Type Adjunct Faculty Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Credits Per Year 2–12 Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
