    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14701": {
      "title": "Adjunct Athletic Training Faculty",
      "description": "Gannon University | Adjunct Athletic Training Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Athletic Training Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All courses are taught according to the predetermined design, content, and Student Learning Objectives to ensure compliance with CAATE Curricular Content Standards. Courses may include programmatic assessment tools or which the adjunct will share responsibility for reporting. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Adjunct Athletic Training Faculty Posting Number AP071 Division School of Health Professions Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Adjunct Faculty may teach 1-2 courses within the MAT curriculum. The content and number of courses taught may depend on the expertise of the adjunct and current faculty. Courses are 8-week sessions, most of which meet 4 days per week for 2 hours each day. Many courses include lab and lecture. If adjunct candidates are interested in teaching more than one class, effort may be made to minimize the number of courses taught in the same 8-week session to reduce the required time commitment and permit sufficient preparation for classes. Required Qualifications Athletic Training BOC Certification PA State License Able to teach graduate students in face-to-face didactic and lab settings on a daily basis throughout the course. Must be familiar with, or able to learn, how to use Blackboard Ultra, or other LMS , to manage courses. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching graduate or undergraduate students. Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a normal academic environment. Must be able to demonstrate clinical skills and equipment usage related to assigned course. WORKING CONDITIONS Work is performed in a normal classroom/lab and office setting. Tenure Status Temporary Position Type Adjunct Faculty Employment Status Part-Time Position Length N/A Credits Per Year 3-6 Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Optional Documents Transcripts Teaching Statement Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
