      "description": "Gannon University | Adjunct Faculty, Speech-Language Pathology Program (Ruskin, FL) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Speech-Language Pathology Program (Ruskin, FL) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Speech-Language Pathology Program (Ruskin, FL) Posting Number AP023 Division School of Health Professions Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Ruskin, Fl Position Summary Gannon University’s Morosky College of Health Professions and Sciences is seeking qualified adjuncts to teach in traditional areas of speech-languaga pathology for the Graduate Speech-Language Pathology Program at Ruskin, Florida. Candidates with expertise in the following advanced topics are encouraged to apply: Clinical Methods, Motor Speech Disorders, Swallowing Disorders, Fluency Disorders, Hearing Disorders and Aural Rehabilitation. Successful candidates must (1) have a master’s degree; preferably a higher degree such as PhD, Ed.D., AuD, or SLPD , (2) demonstrate excellence in teaching, (3) have some experience using technology in teaching, and (4) must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Required Qualifications Candidates require at least a Master’s degree in the relevant discipline (Communication Sciences and Disorders, Audiology or Speech-Language Pathology) with teaching or professional experience. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a normal academic environment. WORKING CONDITIONS Work is performed in a normal classroom and office setting. Tenure Status Temporary Position Type Adjunct Faculty Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 5M Credits Per Year 2-15 Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Optio