      "description": "Gannon University | Adjunct Faculty - Cybersecurity Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty - Cybersecurity Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Adjunct Faculty - Cybersecurity Posting Number AP009 Division School of Engineering and Computing Department Col. of Engineering & Business Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Gannon University’s School of Engineering and Computing ( SEC ) is seeking to expand its pool of qualified adjuncts for its undergraduate and graduate Cybersecurity programs offered by the department of Computer and Information Science. Required Qualifications Candidates interested in leading graduate courses must have an earned Doctorate from a related discipline. Candidates interested in the undergraduate courses must have a Master’s degree in the relevant discipline with teaching or professional experience. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a normal academic environment. WORKING CONDITIONS Work is performed in a normal classroom and office setting. Tenure Status Temporary Position Type Adjunct Faculty Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 5M Credits Per Year 1-4 Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
